 Rom.6:12, al.; in questions, Mat.13:28, Mrk.15:12, Jhn.8:[5], Rom.6:1, al.; continuing a narrative or resuming it after a digression, Mat.1:17, Luk.3:18, Jhn.1:22 2:18 (and very frequently in this Gospel), Act.26:22, al.; ἄρα οὖν (see: ἄρα); ἐπεὶ οὖν, Heb.2:14; οὖν with ptcp. (= ἐπεὶ οὖν), Act.2:30, Rom.5:1, al.; ἐὰν οὖν (where οὖν rather in sense belongs to the apodosis), Mat.5:23, Luk.4:7, Jhn.6:62, Rom.2:26, al.; ὡς οὖν, Jhn.4:1, al. \n (AS)","source_line":3885}],"occurrence_count":494,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"pois","count":295},{"gloss":"portanto","count":100},{"gloss":"então","count":89},{"gloss":"isso","count":10}]},"G3992":{"id":"G3992","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G3992","disambiguated_id":"G3992 =","unique_id":"G3992","headword":"πέμπω","transliteration":"pempō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to send","definition_en":"πέμπω \n [in LXX chiefly for שָׁלַח ;] \nto send; \n __(a) of persons: with accusative, absol., Mat.22:7, Luk.7:19, Jhn.1:22, 2Co.9:3, al.; ptcp. before verb., Mat.14:10, Act.19:31, al.; ptcp. before διά (= Heb. יָד;, 1Ki.16:20, al.), Mat.11:2 (cf. Rev.1:1); of teachers sent by God, Jhn.1:33 4:34, Rom.8:3, al.; with accusative and dative, 1Co.4:17, Php.2:19; before πρός, with accusative, Luk.4:26, Jhn.16:7, al.; before λέγων (cf. Heb. אָמַר שָׁלַח Gen.38:25, al.), Luk.7:6, 19; before εἰς, with accusative loc., Mat.2:8, Luk.15:15, al.; before εἰς (of purpose), Eph.6:22, Col.4:8, 1Pe.2:14; with inf., Jhn.1:33, 1Co.16:3, Rev.22:16; \n __(b) of things : Rev.11:10; before εἰς, Rev.1:11; id., of purpose, Act.11:29, Php.4:16; with dative of person(s), 2Th.2:11; π. τ. δρέπανον σου (cf. εξαποστείλατε δρέπανα = מַגָּל שָׁלַח, Jol.3:13), Rev.14:15, 18 (cf. ἀνα-, ἐκ-, μετα-, προ-, συν-πέμπω) \n SYN.: ἀποστέλλω, q.v (AS)","source_line":4114}],"occurrence_count":79,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"enviou","count":26},{"gloss":"enviei","count":9},{"gloss":"envia","count":6},{"gloss":"enviar","count":6},{"gloss":"